The {{NEXT}} block had accumulated ~80 commit-level bullets since 0.002 -- a faithful record but unreadable as a release changelog. Condensed to ~27 grouped bullets under CPAN::Changes [GROUP] headers (Backward Incompatibilities, New Features, Security, Data Loss and Correctness, Interop, Diagnostics, Accepted Limits, Internals). Every SECURITY, DATA-LOSS and breaking BEHAVIOUR CHANGE stays visible and named; the many interop/type fixes are grouped with their ADR/karr refs kept for traceability. The full detailed version stays in git history. The actual release cut remains a maintainer decision.
